printer-driver-captdriver (0.2.1~git20260813.f2d2da8-0caramos1) noble; urgency=medium

  * First CaramOS package of captdriver, the open-source driver for Canon
    CAPT laser printers such as the LBP2900/LBP2900B.
  * Upstream: mounaiban/captdriver, branch 0.2.1-pr at f2d2da8 (2026-08-13),
    the 2026 protocol fixes by ValdikSS staged there for upstream.
  * Decode status replies by payload size (upstream pull request #55 by
    Ershad Kunnakkadan): basic status replies no longer fill the page
    counters with stale or random bytes, which could keep a job from
    printing.
  * Give each PPD the IEEE 1284 device ID of its printer (upstream pull
    request #56), so the automatic printer setup matches every model the
    driver supports exactly. By model name only the LBP2900 and LBP3010 PPDs
    matched: the LBP3000 got the LBP3010 PPD, whose media type numbers mean
    other paper types, and the LBP3100 and LBP6000 got no driver. The LBP3000
    and LBP3100 get PPDs of their own.
  * Shorter model names for the LBP3010 and LBP3100 PPDs, so that their
    ShortNickName fits the 31 characters cupstestppd allows.
  * Install the filter into /usr/lib/cups/filter, where AppArmor lets cupsd
    run it, and build the PPDs with LC_ALL=C.
  * Modaliases for ubuntu-drivers, so CaramOS Driver Check can offer the
    driver for a connected printer.
  * When installed, switch queues that the automatic setup created earlier
    with another driver to this driver, and set up a connected printer that
    has no queue.

 -- Vietnam Linux Family <developer@vietnamlinuxfamily.net>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 01:40:00 +0700
